/-!
# Divisorial sheaves on projective dlt pairs are Cohen–Macaulay

Let `(X, B)` be a dlt pair with `B` an effective `ℚ`-divisor and `X` projective over an
algebraically closed field `k` of characteristic zero, and let `D` be an integral Weil divisor on
`X` which is `ℚ`-Cartier. Then the divisorial sheaf `𝒪_X(D)` is Cohen–Macaulay.

The proof perturbs `B` to a boundary `B₀` with `(X, B₀)` klt. If `mD` is Cartier, a general member
`G` of `|m(A - D)|` for a sufficiently ample `A` gives a klt pair `(X, B₀ + (1 - 1/m)G)`, and the
cyclic cover `p : Y ⟶ X` defined by `⨁_{i<m} 𝒪_X(i(D - A))` is a projective klt variety, hence
Cohen–Macaulay; `𝒪_X(D - A)` is a direct summand of `p_* 𝒪_Y`, and twisting by `A` concludes.

## Main results

* `MMP.Mori.isCMSheaf_divisorialSheaf_of_isDltPair`: for a projective dlt pair `(X, B)` and a
  `ℚ`-Cartier divisor `D`, the sheaf `𝒪_X(D)` is Cohen–Macaulay.

## Implementation notes

* `X` carries its structure morphism `sX : X ⟶ Spec k`; projectivity is
  `MMP.Mori.IsProjectiveVariety k sX`.
* The dlt condition is `MMP.Mori.IsDltPair sX n K B` with a canonical divisor `K` of dimension
  `n`; it includes `0 ≤ B`, so effectivity is not a separate hypothesis.
* `𝒪_X(D)` is `MMP.Mori.Divisor.divisorialSheaf D`, Cohen–Macaulayness of a sheaf is
  `MMP.Mori.IsCMSheaf`, and `D` is `ℚ`-Cartier when `Divisor.toQDivisor D` is
  (`MMP.Mori.QDivisor.IsQCartier`).
* The field of complex numbers is replaced by an algebraically closed field of characteristic
  zero.

## References

* [J. Kollár, S. Mori, *Birational geometry of algebraic varieties*][KollarMori1998], Theorem 5.22
  and Corollary 5.25.
-/

@[expose] public section

section

/-!
## Proof: Divisorial sheaves on projective dlt pairs are Cohen–Macaulay

Let `(X, B)` be a dlt pair, `B` an effective `ℚ`-divisor, on a variety `X` projective over an
algebraically closed field `k` of characteristic zero, and let `D` be a `ℚ`-Cartier divisor.
Then `𝒪_X(D)` is Cohen–Macaulay [KollarMori1998, Cor. 5.25].

Perturb `B` to an effective boundary `B₀` with `(X, B₀)` klt. Let `m > 0` with `mD` Cartier and
choose a Cartier divisor `A` with `m(A - D)` generated by its global sections. For a general
`φ` with `G = div φ + m(A - D)` effective, the pair `(X, B₀ + (1 - 1/m)G)` is klt and the cyclic
cover `p : Y = Spec_X ⊕_{i<m} 𝒪_X(i(D - A)) ⟶ X` is a normal projective variety on which
`(Y, p^*B₀)` is klt. By the projective klt theorem `Y` is Cohen–Macaulay, hence so is
`p_* 𝒪_Y = ⊕_{i<m} 𝒪_X(i(D - A))`, and so is its direct summand `𝒪_X(D - A)`. Twisting by the
invertible `𝒪_X(A)` gives the assertion.

## Main results

* `MMP.Mori.isCMSheaf_divisorialSheaf_of_isDltPair`

## Implementation notes

The cover is shown klt through log discrepancies. With `K_Y = div(p^*ω)` for a rational top form
`ω` with `K_X = div(ω)`, the boundary is `Δ_Y = p^*(K_X + B₀ + (1 - 1/m)G) - K_Y`. A divisorial
valuation of `k(Y)` restricts to a power `v^e` of a divisorial valuation of `k(X)`, and its log
discrepancy for `(Y, Δ_Y)` is `e` times that of `v` for `(X, B₀ + (1 - 1/m)G)`, hence positive.
That `Δ_Y` is effective is a computation along each prime divisor `E'` of `Y`, lying over a prime
divisor `E` of `X` with ramification index `e`: by the tame formula `coeff_{E'} Δ_Y` is
`e · coeff_E(B₀ + (1 - 1/m)G) - (e - 1)`. Near `E` the cover is `Spec 𝒪[t]/(tᵐ - u)` with
`div u = G`. If `E ⊄ G` then `u` is a unit and `m` is invertible, so `tᵐ - u` is separable modulo
the maximal ideal and `e = 1`; if `E` is a reduced component of `G` then `u` is a uniformizer, no
element of `𝒪[t]` has valuation one unless `ord_{E'}(t) = 1`, and `e = m`.

## References

* [J. Kollár, S. Mori, *Birational geometry of algebraic varieties*][KollarMori1998], Theorem 5.22
  and Corollary 5.25.
-/

section

